# Check out every text file with LF on all platforms. rustfmt
# (newline_style = "Unix"), Oxfmt, and the generated-output comparisons work on
# bytes, so a CRLF checkout on Windows would fail them.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
# The generated notices reproduce upstream licence files verbatim, including
# their line endings, and `pnpm notices:check` compares committed bytes with
# regenerated bytes. Normalizing either the artifacts or the curated upstream
# copies would change their digests on a fresh checkout, so they are stored
# byte for byte instead of as normalized text.
legal/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt -text
legal/sources/upstream/** -text
legal/sources/canonical/** -text
legal/sources/native/** -text
